WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.064 --> 00:00:03.950
- [Narrator] This song
might be familiar to you.

00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:05.658
♫ United States, Canada, Mexico, Panama

00:00:05.658 --> 00:00:07.069
♫ Haiti, Jamaica, Peru

00:00:07.069 --> 00:00:08.310
- [Narrator] Okay, well, listen to this.

00:00:08.310 --> 00:00:10.221
♫ United States, Canada, Mexico, Panama

00:00:10.221 --> 00:00:11.784
♫ Haiti, Jamaica, Peru

00:00:11.784 --> 00:00:13.779
♫ Republic Dominican, Cuba, Caribbean

00:00:13.779 --> 00:00:15.050
♫ Greenland, El Salvador, too.

00:00:15.050 --> 00:00:17.147
♫ Puerto Rico, Colombia, Venezuela

00:00:17.147 --> 00:00:20.233
♫ Honduras, Guyana, and still

00:00:20.233 --> 00:00:21.674
- [Narrator] Rob Paulsen has a voice

00:00:21.674 --> 00:00:23.739
that helped define ‘90s cartoons.

00:00:23.739 --> 00:00:25.352
- Egad, Brain, brilliant!

00:00:25.352 --> 00:00:26.978
- Okay, well, let's see, I'm Yakko Warner.

00:00:26.978 --> 00:00:28.384
Hello, nurse!

00:00:28.384 --> 00:00:31.137
I'm also Pinky from Pinky and the Brain.

00:00:31.137 --> 00:00:34.568
And, uh, for those of you who
are fans of Jimmy Neutron,

00:00:34.568 --> 00:00:37.318
I'm Carl, I'm the little fat guy.

00:00:39.045 --> 00:00:40.507
- [Narrator] And you did
Raphael from the original

00:00:40.507 --> 00:00:41.787
Ninja Turtles, right?

00:00:41.787 --> 00:00:43.758
- Yeah, Raphael sounds a lot like me.

00:00:43.758 --> 00:00:46.698
I say things like, "Shredder,
you tin-faced geek,

00:00:46.698 --> 00:00:48.985
"get back here and taste
cold turtle steel!"

00:00:48.985 --> 00:00:52.377
- Okay, we got a couple of
grade-A ding-dongs on our hands.

00:00:52.377 --> 00:00:53.711
- [Narrator] And all the voices,

00:00:53.711 --> 00:00:55.060
they have a background story.

00:00:55.060 --> 00:00:57.980
- Oh no, I feel a flashback coming on.

00:00:57.980 --> 00:00:58.813
- [Narrator] Let's go.

00:00:58.813 --> 00:01:01.563
(cymbal crashes)

00:01:04.227 --> 00:01:07.330
- [Robert] Where did the
inspiration for Pinky come from?

00:01:07.330 --> 00:01:08.866
- We did it, narf!

00:01:08.866 --> 00:01:10.248
We froze the giant!

00:01:10.248 --> 00:01:13.458
- Well, for me, it was a large part

00:01:13.458 --> 00:01:17.020
of my deep abiding love for British humor.

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:18.785
- Here's a little joke for you, Pinky.

00:01:18.785 --> 00:01:19.868
Knock, knock.

00:01:20.833 --> 00:01:23.494
- Well, that's not a
very funny joke, is it?

00:01:23.494 --> 00:01:26.527
- Peter Sellers was a huge
inspiration, but, um, for some reason,

00:01:26.527 --> 00:01:28.531
Mr. Spielberg and his infinite wisdom

00:01:28.531 --> 00:01:30.632
decided it was a good fit
with Maurice LaMarche,

00:01:30.632 --> 00:01:33.463
who was the Brain, so here we are.

00:01:33.463 --> 00:01:34.296
(record scratching)

00:01:34.296 --> 00:01:36.003
- [Narrator] Wait, Steven Spielberg?

00:01:36.003 --> 00:01:37.092
Oh my God, there he is!

00:01:37.092 --> 00:01:38.572
He produced Pinky and the Brain!

00:01:38.572 --> 00:01:40.348
And Animaniacs?

00:01:40.348 --> 00:01:41.196
Wait, wait, wait.

00:01:41.196 --> 00:01:44.357
And he did Saving Private
Ryan, Twister, Men in Black,

00:01:44.357 --> 00:01:47.421
and Schindler's List while
he was making these cartoons.

00:01:47.421 --> 00:01:48.990
(blaring trumpets)

00:01:48.990 --> 00:01:51.408
Okay, IMDB sidetrack over.

00:01:51.408 --> 00:01:53.084
Sorry, back to Rob.

00:01:53.084 --> 00:01:54.251
- Okay, great.

00:01:55.247 --> 00:01:58.144
- [Narrator] Okay, so
Yakko from Animaniacs,

00:01:58.144 --> 00:01:59.558
where did his voice come from?

00:01:59.558 --> 00:02:01.907
- Only our hairdresser knows for sure.

00:02:01.907 --> 00:02:05.737
- They decided on this little
sort of helium-based voice

00:02:05.737 --> 00:02:09.100
that had kind of a smart-
ass vibe a la Groucho Marx.

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:11.344
Hey, Batman, does Dracula know
you're wearing his cape ...

00:02:11.344 --> 00:02:12.177
so badly?

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:15.842
- [Narrator] And as for
the song where he sings

00:02:15.842 --> 00:02:17.998
every country in the world?

00:02:17.998 --> 00:02:19.628
- The interesting thing is it only took me

00:02:19.628 --> 00:02:21.145
one take to record it.

00:02:21.145 --> 00:02:23.133
The song is a beautifully crafted piece.

00:02:23.133 --> 00:02:25.285
That's the difficult part, not singing it.

00:02:25.285 --> 00:02:26.810
♫ Crete, Mauritania, then Transylvania,

00:02:26.810 --> 00:02:28.467
♫ Monaco, Lichtenstein,
Malta and Palestine,

00:02:28.467 --> 00:02:29.837
♫ Fiji, Australia, Sudan.

00:02:29.837 --> 00:02:31.328
- [Narrator] Some other
places you can hear him

00:02:31.328 --> 00:02:34.154
were in Goof Troop, Darkwing Duck,

00:02:34.154 --> 00:02:37.330
Gummi Bears, Tiny Toon Adventures.

00:02:37.330 --> 00:02:38.817
The list goes on.

00:02:38.817 --> 00:02:40.656
This guy is kinda legend.

00:02:40.656 --> 00:02:42.900
- I don't write 'em, and I don't draw 'em.

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:44.258
I'm just the singer.

00:02:44.258 --> 00:02:49.026
But it is a cool thing to be
associated with those shows.

00:02:49.026 --> 00:02:50.777
It's pretty cool, nobody
cares what I look like,

00:02:50.777 --> 00:02:54.110
so I can do it as long as I can breathe.

